(5766479, 837855, 22970, '<td valign="top">Combining three exposures worked really well with this shot. I don''t know if you could have brought out the details in the snow (ground left bottom) as well as you did with only one exposure. I have fav''ed this photograph for several reason. 1) It look very natural and you didn''t go overboard with the editing. 2) You did a great job in picking the location and point of view. 3) I''m not just looking at power lines, I''m enjoying a wonderful landscape image with very nice detail. 4) I can feel the temperature in the photo and wish I was enjoying the snow.<br/> <br/>To sum it up you did what needed to be done to make this work. You did a great job from picking a location, determining to use three exposures, and the out come was great.<br/> <br/>Great job<br/>Scott</td>', 'Combining three exposures worked really well with this shot. I don''t know if you could have brought out the details in the snow (ground left bottom) as well as you did with only one exposure. I have fav''ed this photograph for several reason. 1) It look very natural and you didn''t go overboard with the editing. 2) You did a great job in picking the location and point of view. 3) I''m not just looking at power lines, I''m enjoying a wonderful landscape image with very nice detail. 4) I can feel the temperature in the photo and wish I was enjoying the snow. To sum it up you did what needed to be done to make this work. You did a great job from picking a location, determining to use three exposures, and the out come was great. Great jobScott', '2009-12-14 08:55:39.000000', NULL, 0),
